Name: l-uq
Version: 2.0.0
Date: 2026-08-07
Title: L-Moments Based Uncertainty Quantification from Scarce Samples Including Extremes
Author: Deepan Jayaraman <deepanjayram@gmail.com>, Palaniappan Ramu <palramu@iitm.ac.in>
Maintainer: Deepan Jayaraman <deepanjayram@gmail.com>
Description: Distribution identification and parameter estimation from
 sample L-moments, aimed at small samples that contain genuine extreme
 observations. Identifies a distribution family by its position on the
 L-moment ratio diagram, estimates the parameters of nine families in
 closed form with explicit domain guards and a ranked fallback,
 quantifies identification uncertainty by bootstrap, and scores fits
 against data by Jensen-Shannon divergence and the Kolmogorov-Smirnov
 statistic. This is the GNU Octave packaging of the MATLAB toolbox; the
 sources are shared, and a Python implementation is distributed
 separately on PyPI as lmoments-uq.
Categories: Statistics
Problems: none known
Url: https://github.com/DeepanJayaraman/L-UQ
Depends: octave (>= 6.1.0)
License: MIT
